(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["play-screen"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">On the player<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">The play screen<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">Every part of the play screen in both interfaces: decks, waveforms, key, tempo, notices and the top bar.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>The play screen is where you spend the set. XZ Mods gives you two ways to draw it. MODERN replaces the whole screen with its own layout. CLASSIC keeps the player's own screen and adds a row of buttons, the playing key and the stem rows to it. You choose between them in MODS under <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> (see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/a>).<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-modern-play-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-modern-play-screen\" data-iface=\"modern\">The MODERN play screen <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>MODERN draws every deck the same way: a top bar across the screen, one waveform lane per deck with a narrow info column on its left, a row of hot-cue lamps, and a deck strip at the bottom. Two decks share the screen in halves. For four decks, see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"The MODERN play screen\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-play-zoom-time\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-play-zoom-time.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-play-zoom-time.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"5.972\" data-title=\"The MODERN play screen\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 6 clicks clockwise<\/li><li data-t=\"1700\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 6 clicks anticlockwise<\/li><li data-t=\"2900\">Tap <strong>TIME 1<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3420\">Tap <strong>TIME 1<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3940\">Tap <strong>INFO HEADER<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4460\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-top-bar\" data-anchor=\"top-bar\" data-iface=\"modern\">Top bar <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Top bar\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-four-stems\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-four-stems.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-four-stems.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.772\" data-title=\"Top bar\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Tap <strong>DECKS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1020\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 1 click clockwise, then push it<\/li><li data-t=\"1720\">Tap <strong>STEMS HEADER<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2240\">Tap <strong>STEMS HEADER<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-1\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · TOP BAR<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Deck 1 is the master, deck 2 plays in a 4-beat loop with KEY SYNC holding its key.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"14.000\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"1: SINGLE\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"20.000\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"2: A. HOT CUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"27.750\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"3: A. CUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"47.500\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"4: BEAT FX\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"70.375\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"5: DECKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"81.250\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"6: INFO\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"88.500\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"7: STEMS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"96.500\" data-y=\"8.333\" aria-label=\"8: MODS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-1-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Deck 1 is the master, deck 2 plays in a 4-beat loop with KEY SYNC holding its key.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>SINGLE<\/b> <span>CONTINUE | PLAY MODE. The lit word is what a deck does at the end of a track: SINGLE stops, CONTINUE loads the next track in the list and plays it. Tap to switch.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>A. HOT CUE<\/b> <span>Lit while HOT CUE AUTO LOAD is on. Red means every track brings its hot cues, white means only the tracks marked for it in the library. Tap to step through ON, the library setting and OFF.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>A. CUE<\/b> <span>Lit while AUTO CUE is on, so the cue point lands where the music starts. Tap to switch it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>BEAT FX<\/b> <span>The effect, its beat and time, the FX BPM and the channel it is on. It fills red while the effect is on.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>DECKS<\/b> <span>Shows which decks the sides drive and opens DECK VIEW. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>INFO<\/b> <span>Opens INFO for the active deck's track.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>STEMS<\/b> <span>Steps the stem buttons through their layouts. Lit blue while stems are on. In 4 DECKS it shows or hides them. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-play-screen-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>MODS<\/b> <span>Opens MODS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>A lamp label in grey shows a mode the player does not let XZ Mods change from the screen. Change it in the player's own UTILITY instead (hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span>). You can hide the three lamps in MODS under <strong>SCREEN<\/strong>, <strong>LAMPS AND TITLES<\/strong>. The BEAT FX readout then takes their room.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-2\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/432f61bdd96e35a3.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: ECHO on: the readout fills red, with the beat, the time in milliseconds and the FX BPM\"><img src=\"manual/shots/432f61bdd96e35a3.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>ECHO on: the readout fills red, with the beat, the time in milliseconds and the FX BPM<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b11b190737bfc626.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: PING PONG chosen but off: a quiet outline\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b11b190737bfc626.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>PING PONG chosen but off: a quiet outline<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6541f782e89f6450.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: An effect without beats shows its name alone\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6541f782e89f6450.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>An effect without beats shows its name alone<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/72cd88bb71a61637.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: VINYL BRAKE with a long time and the FX BPM set by TAP\"><img src=\"manual/shots/72cd88bb71a61637.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>VINYL BRAKE with a long time and the FX BPM set by TAP<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The first moments after start, before the effect has been read\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The first moments after start, before the effect has been read<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden: the readout starts at the left edge\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden: the readout starts at the left edge<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/fa14e55f7a57bdb1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The same with ECHO on\"><img src=\"manual/shots/fa14e55f7a57bdb1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The same with ECHO on<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-deck-column-and-waveform-lanes\" data-anchor=\"deck-column-and-waveform-lanes\" data-iface=\"modern\">Deck column and waveform lanes <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-3\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · DECKS AND LANES<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Each deck gets an info column and a scrolling waveform. The playhead is the red line in the middle.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"13.500\" data-y=\"7.917\" aria-label=\"1: DECK tag\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"13.500\" data-y=\"12.917\" aria-label=\"2: Source\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"13.500\" data-y=\"21.875\" aria-label=\"3: Key\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"9.375\" data-y=\"41.458\" aria-label=\"4: KEY SYNC\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"13.500\" data-y=\"46.250\" aria-label=\"5: Tuning\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"11.000\" data-y=\"51.667\" aria-label=\"6: ORIGINAL\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"60.250\" data-y=\"9.167\" aria-label=\"7: Beat countdown\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"35.250\" data-y=\"27.917\" aria-label=\"8: Bar number\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"22.250\" data-y=\"33.750\" aria-label=\"9: Loop\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"54.500\" data-y=\"20.833\" aria-label=\"10: Playhead\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-10\">10<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"11\" data-x=\"87.500\" data-y=\"52.708\" aria-label=\"11: ZOOM\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-11\">11<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"12\" data-x=\"30.625\" data-y=\"57.708\" aria-label=\"12: Hot-cue lamps\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-3-12\">12<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Each deck gets an info column and a scrolling waveform. The playhead is the red line in the middle.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DECK tag<\/b> <span>Tap to make this the active deck. The blue tile marks the active deck. The dashes beside the name count the beats of the bar.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Source<\/b> <span>Where the track came from: USB1 or USB2.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Key<\/b> <span>The key the deck plays now. Green or amber means it mixes with the master deck's key. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"play-screen\" data-anchor=\"key-and-key-sync\">Key<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>KEY SYNC<\/b> <span>Replaces the KEY caption while KEY SYNC holds this deck's key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Tuning<\/b> <span>How many cents the playing key sits off the nearest semitone.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>ORIGINAL<\/b> <span>The track's analysed key, shown once the playing key has moved away from it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Beat countdown<\/b> <span>Bars and beats to the next cue ahead of the playhead, as bars.beats.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Bar number<\/b> <span>Counts bars every four bars, so you can count phrases.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>Loop<\/b> <span>A running loop shades the waveform and names its length.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>Playhead<\/b> <span>The current position. The waveform scrolls past it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"11\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-11\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">11<\/span><div><b>ZOOM<\/b> <span>How far the waveforms are zoomed. Turn the rotary encoder to zoom in or out.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"12\" id=\"f-play-screen-3-12\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">12<\/span><div><b>Hot-cue lamps<\/b> <span>Pads A to H in their cue colours. A dark lamp is an empty pad.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Turn the rotary encoder on the play screen to zoom both lanes together. There are seven zoom steps. The zoom is kept when you leave the screen, and saved to the USB with your other settings.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-4\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/71f3d749377facb2.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Zoomed fully in on deck 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/71f3d749377facb2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Zoomed fully in on deck 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/db600f7f400a5abb.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Zoomed fully out\"><img src=\"manual/shots/db600f7f400a5abb.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Zoomed fully out<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/aa5f1a15ccd05378.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: WAVEFORM CURRENT POSITION set to LEFT: more of what is coming up. This choice is saved to the USB too\"><img src=\"manual/shots/aa5f1a15ccd05378.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>WAVEFORM CURRENT POSITION set to LEFT: more of what is coming up. This choice is saved to the USB too<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-deck-strip\" data-anchor=\"deck-strip\" data-iface=\"modern\">Deck strip <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-5\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · DECK STRIP<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The two deck strips. Deck 1 is the tempo master, deck 2 is synced to it.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"3.750\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"1: DECK badge\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"31.250\" data-y=\"63.125\" aria-label=\"2: Title and artist\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"46.000\" data-y=\"62.917\" aria-label=\"3: Play state\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"6.500\" data-y=\"71.875\" aria-label=\"4: TRACK\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"18.750\" data-y=\"79.167\" aria-label=\"5: REMAIN / TIME\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"26.875\" data-y=\"65.208\" aria-label=\"6: QUANTIZE\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"37.125\" data-y=\"65.208\" aria-label=\"7: Tempo range\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"32.750\" data-y=\"78.125\" aria-label=\"8: MT\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"87.500\" data-y=\"78.125\" aria-label=\"9: SYNC\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"49.875\" data-y=\"72.917\" aria-label=\"10: BPM\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-10\">10<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"11\" data-x=\"23.750\" data-y=\"82.292\" aria-label=\"11: Cue marks\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-11\">11<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"12\" data-x=\"25.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"12: Overview\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-12\">12<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"13\" data-x=\"14.000\" data-y=\"97.917\" aria-label=\"13: Minute scale\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-5-13\">13<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The two deck strips. Deck 1 is the tempo master, deck 2 is synced to it.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DECK badge<\/b> <span>The deck this strip belongs to, lit when it is the active deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Title and artist<\/b> <span>The loaded track.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Play state<\/b> <span>A triangle while the deck plays, two bars while it is paused.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>TRACK<\/b> <span>The track's number in the list it was loaded from.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>REMAIN / TIME<\/b> <span>The lit word says how the time counts: REMAIN counts down to the end, TIME counts up from the start. Tap the time to switch.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>QUANTIZE<\/b> <span>Red while QUANTIZE is on, with the beat value loops and cues snap to.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Tempo range<\/b> <span>The tempo slider's range, for example ±10.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>MT<\/b> <span>MASTER TEMPO. It blinks while KEY SYNC holds the key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>SYNC<\/b> <span>Lit while the deck is synced.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>BPM<\/b> <span>The deck's playing BPM. MASTER marks the tempo master.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"11\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-11\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">11<\/span><div><b>Cue marks<\/b> <span>Hot cues as lettered chips and memory cues as red marks above the overview.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"12\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-12\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">12<\/span><div><b>Overview<\/b> <span>The whole track. The lighter part is what has played.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"13\" id=\"f-play-screen-5-13\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">13<\/span><div><b>Minute scale<\/b> <span>Minutes to the end in REMAIN, from the start in TIME.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>In the last 30 seconds of a track the overview's playing address flashes slowly, and in the last 15 seconds it flashes fast, in either time mode.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-6\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/538e1acc7a9f46de.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 1 in its last 12 seconds, the end warning flashing\"><img src=\"manual/shots/538e1acc7a9f46de.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 1 in its last 12 seconds, the end warning flashing<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ca3f4fb89ad425a6.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 2 with no track: Not Loaded. in its lane and strip\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ca3f4fb89ad425a6.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 2 with no track: Not Loaded. in its lane and strip<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b66b4526b7c33c05.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A three-digit track number\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b66b4526b7c33c05.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A three-digit track number<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/11a7f69281909469.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: TIME MODE that you can switch by touch: the lit word is white\"><img src=\"manual/shots/11a7f69281909469.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>TIME MODE that you can switch by touch: the lit word is white<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/9e370e76b7585671.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The first frame after start, before anything has been read: dashes everywhere\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9e370e76b7585671.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The first frame after start, before anything has been read: dashes everywhere<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-key-and-key-sync\" data-anchor=\"key-and-key-sync\" data-iface=\"modern\">Key and KEY SYNC <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>The large key in each deck's column is the key the deck plays right now. Tempo with MASTER TEMPO off, a key shift and KEY SYNC all move it. Its colour compares it with the master deck's key. Green means it mixes with the master's key: the same key, its relative major or minor, or one step away on the key wheel, tuned within 25 cents of the master. Amber means it would mix, but it is detuned by more than 25 cents. White means neither, and the master deck itself is always white. Turn KEY MATCH COLOURS off in <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> and every key is white. The cents beside it show how far it sits off the semitone, so you can match by ear. Once the playing key leaves the track's analysed key, ORIGINAL shows the analysed key below it.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Key and KEY SYNC\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"key-shift-sync\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/key-shift-sync.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/key-shift-sync.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"8.252\" data-title=\"Key and KEY SYNC\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>PLAY<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>KEYS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> to <strong>KEY UP<\/strong> and push it<\/li><li data-t=\"2860\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> to <strong>KEY DOWN<\/strong> and push it<\/li><li data-t=\"5760\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> to <strong>RESET<\/strong> and push it<\/li><li data-t=\"6420\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> to <strong>KEY SYNC<\/strong> and push it<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<p>While KEY SYNC holds a deck's key, the KEY caption becomes a blue <strong>KEY SYNC<\/strong> chip and the deck's <strong>MT<\/strong> lamp blinks, half a second lit and half a second dark.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-7\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: KEY SYNC holds Bbm, MT lit\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>KEY SYNC holds Bbm, MT lit<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ba22f219e129ed1f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Half a second later, MT dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ba22f219e129ed1f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Half a second later, MT dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: MASTER TEMPO off: +2.20 % lifts A minor by 38 cents, still Am\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>MASTER TEMPO off: +2.20 % lifts A minor by 38 cents, still Am<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: At +6.10 % the playing key reaches Bbm\"><img src=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>At +6.10 % the playing key reaches Bbm<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Keys written as wheel numbers, with a key shift on deck 1\"><img src=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Keys written as wheel numbers, with a key shift on deck 1<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/bd40c8505412c50f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The whole play screen with wheel-number keys\"><img src=\"manual/shots/bd40c8505412c50f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The whole play screen with wheel-number keys<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6006460a8c5e74a9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: An older loader without the analysed key: the key and its key-shift step\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6006460a8c5e74a9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>An older loader without the analysed key: the key and its key-shift step<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d088e6ddb1537187.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: No key read on deck 1, and a key name too long for the large face on deck 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d088e6ddb1537187.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>No key read on deck 1, and a key name too long for the large face on deck 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>You choose how keys are written (as on the USB, musical or wheel numbers) and whether the playing key shows at all in MODS under <strong>SCREEN<\/strong>. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-waveform-colours\" data-anchor=\"waveform-colours\" data-iface=\"modern\">Waveform colours <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>MODS under <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> offers four waveform colours for MODERN. They change the lanes and the overviews together. Your choice is saved to the USB. <strong>3-BAND COLOURS<\/strong>, beside LAMPS AND TITLES, changes the colour of each band; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-band colours<\/a>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Waveform colours\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-play-colours\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-play-colours.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-play-colours.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"8.772\" data-title=\"Waveform colours\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>SCREEN<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>STOCK<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Tap <strong>RGB<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2560\">Tap <strong>3-BAND<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3080\">Tap <strong>STEMS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3600\">Tap <strong>LAMPS AND TITLES<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4120\">Tap <strong>MODE LAMPS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4640\">Tap <strong>QUANTIZE LAMP<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5160\">Tap <strong>TITLES IN WAVEFORMS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5680\">Tap <strong>DECK + WAVE<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"6200\">Tap <strong>DECK ONLY<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"6720\">Tap <strong>OFF<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"7240\">Tap <strong>CLOSE<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>What you see<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>STOCK<\/td><td>One blue waveform with white peaks<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>RGB<\/td><td>Lows red, mids green, highs blue<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3-BAND<\/td><td>Lows blue, mids amber, highs white, or the colours you chose in <strong>3-BAND COLOURS<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS<\/td><td>Drums, harmonics and vocals in their stem colours. A track without stems shows 3-BAND<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-8\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/18af45b0d42b0901.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: STOCK\"><img src=\"manual/shots/18af45b0d42b0901.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>STOCK<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/640b52024d9c2371.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: RGB\"><img src=\"manual/shots/640b52024d9c2371.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>RGB<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 3-BAND\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>3-BAND<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2c7095f092d37814.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: STEMS\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2c7095f092d37814.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>STEMS<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p><strong>USB COLORS<\/strong> (MODS, <strong>SCREEN<\/strong>, <strong>LAMPS AND TITLES<\/strong>) lets each deck take the colours saved on the USB stick its track came from.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-9\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/844f5cd9b31a5554.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECK + WAVE: the deck tile takes the stick&#x27;s colour and the waveform the stick&#x27;s waveform colour\"><img src=\"manual/shots/844f5cd9b31a5554.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECK + WAVE: the deck tile takes the stick's colour and the waveform the stick's waveform colour<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/da7b23a580de3b5c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECK ONLY: only the deck tile takes the stick&#x27;s colour\"><img src=\"manual/shots/da7b23a580de3b5c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECK ONLY: only the deck tile takes the stick's colour<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: OFF: every deck uses the player&#x27;s own colours\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>OFF: every deck uses the player's own colours<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-notices\" data-anchor=\"notices\" data-iface=\"modern\">Notices <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>When something you asked for does not happen, a notice appears in the middle of the screen for two and a half seconds. It says what went wrong in one line, for example <strong>DECK 1 DID NOT LOAD THE TRACK<\/strong>. A long notice wraps. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"troubleshooting\">Messages and troubleshooting<\/a> explains each one.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Notices\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-choose-track-error\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-choose-track-error.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-choose-track-error.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"4.792\" data-title=\"Notices\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Tap <strong>DECKS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1020\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 1 click clockwise, then push it<\/li><li data-t=\"1720\">Tap <strong>CHOOSE TRACK<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2240\">Push <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"2740\">Tap <strong>TRACK ROW<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3260\">Tap <strong>LOAD DECK 3<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-10\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/0b2dd61190edad2d.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A notice over the lanes\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0b2dd61190edad2d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A notice over the lanes<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/70bbc985a0f785ef.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A long notice\"><img src=\"manual/shots/70bbc985a0f785ef.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A long notice<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c0bd530e4a795be1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The same screen once the notice has gone\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c0bd530e4a795be1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The same screen once the notice has gone<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>If a deck cannot go on, its lane turns red and names the problem, for example <strong>EMERGENCY LOOP<\/strong> (the deck loops until you load a track) or <strong>CANNOT READ THE TRACK<\/strong> with the player's error code. Tap <strong>CHOOSE TRACK<\/strong> on the red band to make that deck active and open BROWSE.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-11\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/709966e3cc33a46d.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: EMERGENCY LOOP on deck 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/709966e3cc33a46d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>EMERGENCY LOOP on deck 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c6266a54d7583b0b.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: CANNOT READ THE TRACK with error E-8302\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c6266a54d7583b0b.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>CANNOT READ THE TRACK with error E-8302<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>A deck that plays its whole track from RAM after the music USB went out is not in trouble, so its lane says so in teal instead: <strong>WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE<\/strong>, in the waveform's place. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"when-the-music-usb-goes-out\">RAM tracks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-shortcut\" data-anchor=\"shortcut\" data-iface=\"modern\">SHORTCUT <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shortcut\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shortcut.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"114.93\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHORTCUT<\/span><\/span> on the play screen to see the settings you change most during a set on one page. It has the same four groups as the player's own SHORTCUT screen: PLAYER SETTINGS, DECK STATUS, DEVICE SETTINGS and MY SETTINGS. Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span> or tap the arrow in the top left corner to return to the play screen.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"SHORTCUT\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"shortcut\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/shortcut.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/shortcut.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.912\" data-title=\"SHORTCUT\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"shortcut\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/shortcut.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"114.93\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">SHORTCUT<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 1 click clockwise, then push it<\/li><li data-t=\"1700\">Turn <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rotary\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rotary.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"33\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">ROTARY SELECTOR<\/span><\/span> 1 click clockwise, then push it<\/li><li data-t=\"2400\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-12\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">SHORTCUT<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/e17b78dfff19adc7.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The SHORTCUT screen with quantize, waveform and time settings for both decks.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"25.625\" data-y=\"14.167\" aria-label=\"1: Highlighted row\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"15.625\" data-y=\"27.083\" aria-label=\"2: Locked value\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"30.000\" data-y=\"36.250\" aria-label=\"3: Choice buttons\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"53.750\" data-y=\"19.167\" aria-label=\"4: DECK 1 lamps\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"93.125\" data-y=\"10.208\" aria-label=\"5: LINK lamp\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"60.000\" data-y=\"41.667\" aria-label=\"6: Jumps\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"25.000\" data-y=\"58.333\" aria-label=\"7: DEVICE SETTINGS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"75.000\" data-y=\"61.458\" aria-label=\"8: MY SETTINGS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-12-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The SHORTCUT screen with quantize, waveform and time settings for both decks.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Highlighted row<\/b> <span>Turn the encoder to move between rows. The line under the title explains the highlighted row.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Locked value<\/b> <span>A lock and READ ONLY HERE mean XZ Mods shows this value but cannot change it here. Pushing or tapping it does nothing.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Choice buttons<\/b> <span>Tap a value to change it. The lit button is the current value.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>DECK 1 lamps<\/b> <span>QUANTIZE (or Q1), SYNC, SLIP, MASTER and the time mode for deck 1. Tap QUANTIZE to switch it, tap REMAIN or TIME to change the time mode.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>LINK lamp<\/b> <span>Shows whether the player is linked to other players.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Jumps<\/b> <span>TRACK, PLAYLIST and SEARCH open those lists. MATCHING opens matching tracks, or hands over to the player's own browser when XZ Mods cannot list them.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>DEVICE SETTINGS<\/b> <span>Waveform colour, playhead position, key display format and waveform zoom. These change the MODERN screen at once.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-play-screen-12-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>MY SETTINGS<\/b> <span>Time mode, play mode and auto cue for the decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Which rows you can change depends on what the player lets XZ Mods write. A locked row shows its value and the reason it is read-only. A short <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> on SHORTCUT opens MODS.<\/p>\n<p>NEEDLE LOCK appears in PLAYER SETTINGS when the player reports it. LOCK prevents a waveform touch from searching a playing deck. Pause the deck to search, or choose UNLOCK when that setting is writable.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-play-screen-13\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2863154e9f018a18.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: HOT CUE AUTO LOAD has choices; QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE and AUTO CUE LEVEL are read-only in this fixture\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2863154e9f018a18.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>HOT CUE AUTO LOAD has choices; QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE and AUTO CUE LEVEL are read-only in this fixture<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/a7526c2e4e7e84d5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE as four choices, play mode and auto cue locked\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a7526c2e4e7e84d5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>QUANTIZE BEAT VALUE as four choices, play mode and auto cue locked<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/45c9e476db52ad5f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The waveform colour row with STEMS chosen\"><img src=\"manual/shots/45c9e476db52ad5f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The waveform colour row with STEMS chosen<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c2d897032f0f74c7.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The player&#x27;s own settings shown as values while it is not accepting changes. DEVICE SETTINGS still change the MODERN screen\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c2d897032f0f74c7.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The player's own settings shown as values while it is not accepting changes. DEVICE SETTINGS still change the MODERN screen<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>With four decks, SHORTCUT also shows DECK SELECT. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-classic-play-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-classic-play-screen\" data-iface=\"classic\">The CLASSIC play screen <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>CLASSIC keeps the player's own play screen, so every stock element stays where the XDJ-XZ operating instructions put it. XZ Mods restyles it in the classic theme you chose and adds a row of buttons across the top, the playing key under each deck's key, and stem rows under the waveforms.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"classic\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"The CLASSIC play screen\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"classic-stems\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/classic-stems.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/classic-stems.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"3.072\" data-title=\"The CLASSIC play screen\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Tap the screen<\/li><li data-t=\"1020\">Tap the screen<\/li><li data-t=\"1540\">Tap the screen<\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-14\" data-iface=\"classic\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · CLASSIC<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/770026c35ce8a2ba.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The ORIGINAL theme with stems on in the BELOW / HALF layout. Deck 1&#x27;s playing key has moved from 2A to 11A.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"15.000\" data-y=\"2.083\" aria-label=\"1: VJ.TOOLS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"27.500\" data-y=\"6.250\" aria-label=\"2: DECKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"55.000\" data-y=\"6.250\" aria-label=\"3: Metrics\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"84.750\" data-y=\"6.250\" aria-label=\"4: STEMS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"98.625\" data-y=\"5.833\" aria-label=\"5: MODS\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"13.750\" data-y=\"29.167\" aria-label=\"6: Playing key\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"13.750\" data-y=\"58.333\" aria-label=\"7: Same key\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"31.250\" aria-label=\"8: Stem rows\" aria-describedby=\"f-play-screen-14-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The ORIGINAL theme with stems on in the BELOW / HALF layout. Deck 1's playing key has moved from 2A to 11A.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>VJ.TOOLS<\/b> <span>Switches to the VJ.Tools screen when a VJ.Tools computer is connected. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\">Connect and DJ profiles<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>DECKS<\/b> <span>Shows which decks the sides drive and opens DECK VIEW. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Metrics<\/b> <span>The player's CPU load, free memory and temperature. Tap METRICS to set it up. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"extras\">Extras<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>STEMS<\/b> <span>Steps the stem rows through their layouts. The marks under the label show the current one. Dark in 4 DECKS, which has no stem rows. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>MODS<\/b> <span>Opens MODS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Playing key<\/b> <span>Shown under the player's own key. The analysed key, an arrow, then the key the deck plays now, with its tuning in cents.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Same key<\/b> <span>When the playing key has not moved, KEY and the key, with the cents.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-play-screen-14-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Stem rows<\/b> <span>VOCALS, DRUMS, HARMONICS and BYPASS for each deck. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>This picture is the stock screen of a real player with the XZ Mods buttons and stem rows added. Everything else on it is the player's own: the deck tabs, source, key, BEAT FX, ZOOM, the deck strips with A.HOTCUE, A.CUE, QUANTIZE, TEMPO and the BPM box. The XDJ-XZ operating instructions explain those.<\/p>\n<p>The key line replaces the player's beat countdown under the key. You choose the key notation and whether the playing key shows in MODS under <strong>SCREEN<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-play-screen-15\" data-iface=\"classic\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">PLAY · CLASSIC, FULL ROWS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b9fbaf344322c2fb.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"An earlier capture with stems in the BELOW / FULL layout, the rows taller with room for the stem level bars. Stem colours here follow an older default. Today drums are blue and harmonics red; see Stem colours.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><\/div><\/div><figcaption>An earlier capture with stems in the BELOW / FULL layout, the rows taller with room for the stem level bars. Stem colours here follow an older default. Today drums are blue and harmonics red; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\" data-anchor=\"stem-colours\">Stem colours<\/a>.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<h4 id=\"m-scrolling-waveform\" data-anchor=\"scrolling-waveform\" data-iface=\"classic\">Scrolling waveform <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>In CLASSIC, <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> offers three scrolling waveforms. The setting is <code>wave_mode<\/code> on the USB.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"classic\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Scrolling waveform\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-classic-wave-choices\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-classic-wave-choices.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-classic-wave-choices.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"9.812\" data-title=\"Scrolling waveform\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>SCREEN<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>CLASSIC<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Tap <strong>2 DECKS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2560\">Tap <strong>4 DECKS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3080\">Tap <strong>4 DECKS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3600\">Tap <strong>STOCK<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4120\">Tap <strong>3-BAND<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"4640\">Tap <strong>STEMS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5160\">Tap <strong>AS ON THE USB<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"5680\">Tap <strong>MUSICAL<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"6200\">Tap <strong>WHEEL<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"6720\">Tap <strong>PLAYING KEY<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"7240\">Tap <strong>KEY MATCH COLOURS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"7760\">Tap <strong>KEY BEFORE TITLE<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"8280\">Tap <strong>CLOSE<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>What you see<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>STOCK<\/td><td>The player's own scrolling waveform<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3-BAND<\/td><td>Layered lows, mids and highs (the default). <strong>3-BAND COLOURS<\/strong> chooses their colours; see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-band colours<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS<\/td><td>Drums, harmonics and vocals layered in their stem colours. A track without prepared stems shows 3-BAND<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The overview in each deck strip stays the player's own in every choice.<\/p>\n<p>When a deck plays its whole track from RAM after the music USB went out, a teal card in its lane says <strong>WHOLE TRACK IN RAM · PLAYABLE<\/strong> where the waveform was. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"when-the-music-usb-goes-out\">RAM tracks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-if-something-looks-wrong\" data-anchor=\"if-something-looks-wrong\">If something looks wrong<\/h3>\n<div class=\"mn\" data-iface=\"modern\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"If something looks wrong\"><ol class=\"mn-scenes\"><li data-flow=\"nav-a-playing-key\" data-video=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-playing-key.mp4\" data-poster=\"assets/manual/nav/nav-a-playing-key.webp\" data-w=\"1280\" data-h=\"480\" data-seconds=\"5.132\" data-title=\"If something looks wrong\"><ol class=\"mn-steps\"><li data-t=\"500\">Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span><\/li><li data-t=\"1000\">Tap <strong>SCREEN<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"1520\">Tap <strong>PLAYING KEY<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2040\">Tap <strong>PLAYING KEY<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"2560\">Tap <strong>KEY MATCH COLOURS<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3080\">Tap <strong>KEY BEFORE TITLE<\/strong><\/li><li data-t=\"3600\">Tap <strong>CLOSE<\/strong><\/li><\/ol><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>You see<\/th><th>Why<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Dashes instead of numbers<\/td><td>The value has not been read yet, or the deck has no track<\/td><td>Wait a moment, or load a track<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A grey mode lamp that does not react<\/td><td>The player does not let XZ Mods change that mode<\/td><td>Change it in UTILITY (hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span>)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO STEM WAVE YET · 3BAND in a lane<\/td><td>STEMS waveform chosen, but this track's stems are not loaded yet<\/td><td>Wait, or prepare the track's stems. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The key stays white on every deck<\/td><td>No master deck, or KEY MATCH COLOURS is off<\/td><td>Set a tempo master, or turn KEY MATCH COLOURS on in <strong>SCREEN<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>";
